"""Render a verified sharp twelve-qubit algebraic sector minimum."""
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
import json,hashlib
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;v=json.loads((R/'independent-verification.json').read_text());p=json.loads((R/'state-parameters.json').read_text());c=json.loads((R/'candidate-state.json').read_text());value=json.loads((R/'value-definition.json').read_text());k=p['k'];degree=value['degree'];decimal=value['decimal'];assert v['globalOptimalityProven']and v['fullPolynomialIdentityVerified']
for f,h in v['inputSha256'].items():assert hashlib.sha256((R/f).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==h
state=c['stateLatex'];appendix='../algebraic-s6/index.html#n12'if k==6 else'../algebraic-s8-n12/index.html'
def tex(t):return '<div class="proof-equation" data-tex="'+escape(t,quote=True)+'"></div>'
def section(id,title,s):return f'<section class="reference-section" id="{id}"><h2>{title}</h2>{s}</section>'
s=f'<section class="intro"><div class="intro-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Exact algebraic optimum · 4 November 2026</p><h1>Twelve qubits:<br><em>the exact minimum of S<sub>{k}</sub></em></h1><p class="intro-description">The algebraic candidate is now proved globally minimal for arbitrary complex pure symmetric states.</p></div></section>'
t=tex(r'\boxed{\min_{\|\psi\|=1,\,\psi\in\operatorname{Sym}^{12}(\mathbb C^2)}S_'+str(k)+r'(\psi)=s_\star='+decimal[:36]+r'\ldots.}')
t+=f'<p>The exact minimum is algebraic of degree {degree}. The decimal displays its value; the <a href="value-definition.json">minimal polynomial and isolating interval</a> specify the exact number.</p>'+tex(r'|\psi_\star\rangle='+state)
t+=f'<p>The <a href="{appendix}">analytical coefficient construction</a> specifies the isolated root and positive square-root branches. Collective rotations also attain this minimum. A complete classification of equality states is not asserted.</p>'
s+=section('theorem','The sharp minimum',t)
t='<p>For possibly unnormalized Dicke amplitudes, define</p>'+tex(r'c_r=\sqrt{\binom{12}r}\,x_r,\quad q=\sum_{r=0}^{12}\binom{12}r|x_r|^2,\quad P_'+str(k)+r'=q^2S_'+str(k)+r'(\psi/\sqrt q).')
t+='<p>The exact certificate gives</p>'+tex(r'\boxed{q^2(P_'+str(k)+r'-s_\star q^2)=\sum_{B,m}\frac{\mathbf v_{B,m}^{\dagger}H_B\mathbf v_{B,m}}{\binom{2L_B}{m}}\ge0.}')
t+='<p>Every vector has degree four, and every real symmetric matrix is positive definite at the specified real algebraic root. Dividing by the positive factor q⁴ proves the global lower bound. The analytical state attains it, so the bound is sharp.</p>'
t+='<p>The certificate specifies its vectors by a <a href="basis.json" download>rational covariant basis</a>, <a href="kernels.json" download>algebraic vanishing kernels</a>, and rational mixing matrices. The <a href="sos-certificate.json" download>Gram certificate</a> defines the matrix entries by a finite exact linear system over the same real number field.</p>'
s+=section('proof','Proof by an exact algebraic sum of squares',t)
t='<p>The standalone verifier independently checks the ingredients needed for the entire polynomial identity.</p><ol><li><strong>Complete invariant space.</strong> Exact raising- and lowering-operator checks establish covariance. Weight counts and exact highest-weight ranks prove that the real, conjugation-symmetric invariant polynomials of bidegree (4,4) form a 250-dimensional space.</li><li><strong>Exact vanishing.</strong> Every kernel vector vanishes at the analytical state. The target has zero value and zero derivatives in the three independent state parameters, with the bound held fixed. These identities are checked exactly modulo the defining polynomial.</li><li><strong>Exact coefficient equations.</strong> The certificate fixes the free Gram entries as rational numbers and defines the remaining 246 entries by 246 coefficient equations. A rigorous interval matrix solve proves existence and uniqueness.</li><li><strong>Full identity.</strong> The 246 coefficient functionals, together with the four vanishing functionals, give an injective map on the complete 250-dimensional invariant space. Certified nonsingularity proves that agreement on these functionals is equality of the full polynomials, for every complex state.</li><li><strong>Positivity.</strong> Directed-rounding real-ball arithmetic encloses the exact Gram entries and their LDL pivots. Every pivot is strictly positive, so no numerical tolerance assumption enters the inequality.</li></ol>'
t+=tex(r'\dim\mathcal V=\sum_{L=0}^{24}\frac{m_L(m_L+1)}2=250,\qquad246+4=250.')
t+='<details><summary>Certificate verification details</summary>'+f'<p>The certificate has {v["positiveDefiniteGramBlocks"]} positive blocks and {v["squaredForms"]} weighted absolute squares. The verifier uses {v["precisionBits"]}-bit directed-rounding arithmetic. The smallest certified LDL lower endpoint is {v["positiveLDLPivotLowerBound"]:.12g}.</p>'+'<p>The root is isolated by rational bisection, and a nonvanishing derivative certifies uniqueness in the original interval. Positive radicands and normalization are checked separately.</p></details>'
s+=section('verification','Why the finite certificate is a global proof',t)
t='<p>The target is reconstructed directly from reduced Dicke density matrices:</p>'+tex(r'(\rho_t)_{ab}=\sqrt{\binom ta\binom tb}\sum_{j=0}^{12-t}\binom{12-t}j x_{a+j}\overline{x_{b+j}},')+tex(r'P_'+str(k)+r'=\binom{12}{'+str(k)+r'}\sum_{t=0}^{'+str(k)+r'}(-1)^{'+str(k)+r'-t}\binom{'+str(k)+r'}t2^t\operatorname{tr}(\rho_t^2).')
t+='<p>Its invariance, bidegree, conjugation symmetry, exact attainment and stationary constraints are checked independently of the certificate-discovery optimizer.</p>'
s+=section('derivation','Independent target and attainment',t)
t='<p>Install the <a href="requirements.txt">tested python-flint dependency</a>, then run from this proof folder:</p><pre>python3 verify_certificate.py</pre><p>The verifier uses exact rational/algebraic arithmetic and rigorous Arb intervals. It requires no optimizer, NumPy or SciPy. The approximate matrix-solve mode is not used.</p><p><a href="verify_certificate.py">Standalone verifier</a> · <a href="independent-verification.json">Verification report and input hashes</a> · <a href="exact_field.py">Exact field arithmetic</a> · <a href="state-parameters.json">Isolated root and rational recovery</a></p>'
s+=section('reproduce','Reproduce the proof',t)
html=f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Twelve-qubit S{k} exact minimum</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><style>.proof-equation{{overflow-x:auto;margin:1.4rem 0;padding:.4rem 0}}pre{{padding:1rem}}main{{max-width:1100px}}li{{margin:.9rem 0}}details{{margin:1.4rem 0}}</style></head><body><header class="site-header"><a class="wordmark" href="../../index.html#n=12&amp;k={k}&amp;mode=min">← Sector-length catalogue</a><nav><a href="#theorem">Theorem</a><a href="#proof">Proof</a><a href="#reproduce">Verify</a></nav></header><main>'+s+'</main><footer class="site-footer"><a href="../index.html">All proofs and remaining gaps ↗</a></footer><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:true,throwOnError:false,trust:false})));</script></body></html>'
(R/'index.html').write_text(html)
